concepts.explanation:
Network failures can have very small effects, or very big effects. Small failures happen quite often, and they are usually just annoying rather than serious. For example, if a network fails while you are working online, any work you have not saved recently might disappear. Or if you are playing an online game, the game might suddenly stop. Frustrating — but not the end of the world.

Large failures with big effects do not happen as often, but they matter far more. Imagine a bank's network failing. Effects of a large failure could include:

not being able to stream films, radio or TV shows;

not being able to reach money in an online bank account to pay bills or buy food;

not being able to play online games with people around the world;

not being able to make video calls to family.
